    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1512">

                <pb facs="1218" n="1102" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg1102"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 817.51/487.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic"> Brown Brothers and Company and J. W. Seligman and
                        Company to the Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">New York</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-08-02">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 2, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: On behalf of the National Bank of
                    Nicaragua, incorporated, we beg to hand you herewith, for your information, copy
                    of a letter which we have today written to Ernest H. Wands, Esquire, Financial
                    Agent of Nicaragua, and copy of his reply.</p>
                <p>In making the loan to which those letters refer, we assume that the Bank, in case
                    of necessity, will receive the same measure of protection which may be afforded
                    to us in connection with loans heretofore made by us to Nicaragua under the
                    Treasury Bills Agreement of September 1, 1911, and the Supplemental Loan
                    Agreement of March 26, 1912.</p>
                <p>We remain [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Brown Brothers and Company</hi>. <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">J. and W. Seligman and Company</hi>.</closer>




                <xi:include href="d1512-a1.xml" xpointer="d1512-a1"/>
